CPU SNAP regression case with a two-atom Si periodic structure.

The example uses `snap.coeff` for the SNAP coefficients and `snap.param` for
the SNAP parameters.

The coefficient and parameter files are deterministic ABACUS-generated test
fixtures. They are intended only to exercise SNAP parsing, energy, force, and
stress evaluation; they are not transferable or physically validated Si
potentials.

The reference values are generated by ABACUS and checked by the existing
04_FF regression harness.  The large cell keeps periodic image interactions
separate while exercising SNAP energy, force, and stress evaluation.
